### Observability — Prometheus, Jaeger, Grafana
###
### Requires: pnpm dc:up:infra
###
### NOTE: the services do not emit traces or custom metrics yet — the
### OpenTelemetry instrumentation is feature 27. Until then Jaeger shows only
### its own internal spans and Prometheus scrapes only the collector. These
### requests are still worth having: they prove the pipeline is wired, and
### they are the ones you will reuse when the real telemetry arrives.

@prometheus = http://localhost:9090
@jaeger     = http://localhost:16686
@grafana    = http://localhost:3030

### --- Prometheus ---

### Which scrape targets are up? Expect otel-collector = 1.
GET {{prometheus}}/api/v1/query?query=up

### Every metric name currently known to Prometheus
GET {{prometheus}}/api/v1/label/__name__/values

### Target health in detail — the same view as the /targets UI page
GET {{prometheus}}/api/v1/targets

### The collector's own throughput (a useful liveness signal for the pipeline)
GET {{prometheus}}/api/v1/query?query=otelcol_receiver_accepted_spans

### --- Jaeger ---

### Services that have reported traces. Until feature 27 this is Jaeger itself.
GET {{jaeger}}/api/services

### Traces for one service (change the parameter once real services report)
GET {{jaeger}}/api/traces?service=jaeger&limit=5

### --- Grafana ---

### Health — expect { "database": "ok", ... }
GET {{grafana}}/api/health

### Provisioned datasources — Prometheus and Jaeger, wired in feature 4
GET {{grafana}}/api/datasources
Authorization: Basic admin:admin

### Dashboards. Empty until feature 22 commits the dashboard JSON.
GET {{grafana}}/api/search?type=dash-db
Authorization: Basic admin:admin
